@bank all
// Pillar 5 Step 3 (head writer W2): P2 "Who saw what?" (seat H2). A witness's answer to "Ask about the fault" on
// their chat card. Read only after Tomas's word (SHIP.works.said.p2). {time} is when they were there ("22:00"),
// {place} the room ("the junior common room"), {machine} the machine's plain name.
// ask.saw: it was showing then. ask.quiet: it wasn't. ask.mixup: an honest mix-up (their plan had them by a different
// machine); it reads like a sighting and gives no place, so the Roster is how you spot it.
== ask.saw
- It was playing up about {time}. I was in {place}.
- {time}, in {place}. It was at it. Couldn't miss it.
- About {time}. I was in {place}, and {machine} was playing up.
? tier>=colleague
- Oh, it was going at {time}. I was in {place}, trying to read. Trying.   #funny
== ask.quiet
- I was in {place} about {time}. Quiet as anything.
- {time}? I was in {place}. {machine} was fine then.
- Nothing at {time}. I was in {place}. Not a peep.
? tier>=colleague
- Quiet at {time}. I'd have noticed. I notice everything in {place}.   #funny
== ask.mixup
- It was going at {time}! I'm sure of it.
- {time}, it was playing up. Definitely. I think.
- About {time}. Plain as day. I'm certain.
